{"outcome":"built","summary":"I built a three-storey tower with drawers on the bottom storey and an open three-compartment bin on the top. The configurator's check passes with no errors and no mesh clashes.

The tower is a column of full bases at cell (1,0), stacked on levels 0, 1 and 2. The configurator only lets a base stack on a full base, and drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. So the two drawers are in half bases beside the column on the ground storey, at (0,0) and (2,0). The column's own bottom cell holds no drawer.

The joint is bolted and the open edges are capped with solid end caps, except one edge on the bottom storey: a cap there would run into a drawer frame, so it stays open. No cover sits over the top bin, so it stays open. The build is 49 parts, a little over the usual 40, because of the caps on all three storeys.","requirements":[{"requirement":"Three-storey tower","status":"met","evidence":"Full bases piece:1,0,0, piece:1,0,1 and piece:1,0,2 are stacked on levels 0, 1 and 2 and snapped together."},{"requirement":"Drawers on the bottom storey","status":"met","evidence":"drawer:0#0,0#cut and drawer:0#2,0#cut sit in half bases on level 0, on either side of the column's bottom cell. The bottom cell itself, a full base, takes no drawer."},{"requirement":"Open bins on the top storey","status":"met","evidence":"bin:1,0,2~hex-bin-full-div3 is a three-compartment bin in the level-2 base, with no cover over it."}]}
